# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF in the working copy on checkout. For shell scripts that is
# not cosmetic: bash reads the trailing \r as part of the command, so a checked
# out `.sh` breaks in Git Bash locally (CI is unaffected, since Linux checkouts
# get LF either way — which is exactly what makes this the kind of breakage that
# only ever bites the person who wrote it).
*.sh text eol=lf
